The `@objectstack/client` auth examples here call `client.auth.register/login/logout/me`, which currently hit `/api/v1/auth/register|login|logout|me`. `AuthPlugin` forwards `/api/v1/auth/*` to better-auth, whose endpoints are `/sign-up/email`, `/sign-in/email`, `/sign-out`, `/get-session`, etc., so these client calls will 404/misbehave. Either update the client to target better-auth routes, or change this guide to use the documented better-auth endpoints (and clarify the current client compatibility).
```suggestion
// Email sign-up
await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/sign-up/email', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    email: 'user@example.com',
    password: 'password123',
    name: 'John Doe',
  }),
  credentials: 'include',
});

// Email sign-in
const loginResponse = await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/sign-in/email', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    email: 'user@example.com',
    password: 'password123',
  }),
  credentials: 'include',
});

const loginData = await loginResponse.json();
// loginData typically includes session information and/or tokens

// Get current session
const sessionResponse = await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/get-session', {
  method: 'GET',
  credentials: 'include',
});

const session = await sessionResponse.json();

// Sign out
await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/sign-out', {
  method: 'POST',
  credentials: 'include',
});
```

The TypeScript usage snippet duplicates imports as both value and type (won’t compile) and uses the deprecated `@objectstack/spec/hub` entrypoint. Prefer importing runtime schemas from `@objectstack/spec/kernel` and types via `z.infer` or `import type { z }` patterns.
```suggestion
import {
  PluginInstallConfigSchema,
  PluginQualityMetricsSchema,
  PluginRegistryEntrySchema,
  PluginSearchFiltersSchema,
  PluginStatisticsSchema,
  PluginVendorSchema,
} from '@objectstack/spec/kernel';
import type { z } from 'zod';

// Derive TypeScript types from Zod schemas
export type PluginInstallConfig = z.infer<typeof PluginInstallConfigSchema>;
export type PluginQualityMetrics = z.infer<typeof PluginQualityMetricsSchema>;
export type PluginRegistryEntry = z.infer<typeof PluginRegistryEntrySchema>;
export type PluginSearchFilters = z.infer<typeof PluginSearchFiltersSchema>;
export type PluginStatistics = z.infer<typeof PluginStatisticsSchema>;
export type PluginVendor = z.infer<typeof PluginVendorSchema>;

// Validate data
const result = PluginInstallConfigSchema.parse(data);
```

The setup snippet uses the old kernel API (`new ObjectKernel({ plugins: [...] })` + `kernel.start()`), but `ObjectKernel` no longer accepts a `plugins` array and uses `kernel.use()` + `kernel.bootstrap()`. This doc example won’t run as written; update it to the current lifecycle and registration pattern.
```suggestion
const kernel = new ObjectKernel();

// HTTP server (required for auth routes)
kernel.use(
  new HonoServerPlugin({
    port: 3000,
  }),
);

// Authentication plugin
kernel.use(
  new AuthPlugin({
    secret: process.env.AUTH_SECRET,
    baseUrl: 'http://localhost:3000',
  }),
);

await kernel.bootstrap();
```
